  "note": "The case depth check as first written, on the corner photographs O2-FL and O2-BR each through its camera, crossed its STOP: -8.77 per cent on O2-BR (case.depthToWidthErrPct, kept with the photographs' other figures, recorded only). Dan ruled on 5 October 2026, after an independent review, that it judged the wrong quantity: it measured the camera, not the case. The plan (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-05-nes-models.md, Global Constraints, the rows revised that day) now judges the case's depth and height on the design patent's orthographic views (case.patent), against the same 1.5 and 3 per cent, drops the row on the two photographs' heights agreeing, and judges the PAL front on O4 against the patent's front view, on at least two measured ratios."
 },
